on-arrival: ko_media_smear_done = 1; news_headline = "KO-aligned media brands Lewica a de facto ally of PiS"

= A hostile week in the democratic media lane

After another breakdown with KO, the familiar line hardens into a campaign:
Lewica is now described as the force that "objectively helps PiS" whenever it
blocks, conditions or delays a democratic-camp vote.

TVN roundtables and Onet headlines stop debating substance and start testing
one accusation: whether we are a progressive party or only a spoiler with a
social veneer. It is difficult to answer without repeating the frame.

The hit lands unevenly. Metropolitan liberals and professional anti-PiS voters
move away fastest; anti-system audiences mostly treat the fight as elite
theatre and drift further right if no material alternative appears.

- @ko_media_smear_counter
- @ko_media_smear_deescalate
- @ko_media_smear_material

@ko_media_smear_counter
title: Launch an aggressive rebuttal campaign
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Contest the smear directly; hardens the feud and still normalises the accusation.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The media team cannot finance a full rebuttal cycle.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; media_capacity += 2; ko_relation -= 7; p2050_relation -= 2; progressive_credibility -= 2; public_trust -= 2; far_right_agenda += 2; ko_poll_momentum += 0.2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.2; metropolitan_liberals_left_affinity -= 4; liberal_professionals_left_affinity -= 4; anti_establishment_youth_left_affinity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica fights the smear and loses more metropolitan trust"

Our spokespeople answer line by line, clip by clip. The party keeps a public
voice and avoids total narrative collapse, but the rebuttal repeats the KO
frame for another week and turns a coalition quarrel into the main political
story. We look combative, not constructive.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@ko_media_smear_deescalate
title: Seek a ceasefire with KO and mute the conflict
subtitle: Quietly reduce the attack cycle; progressive organisations see retreat and blurred boundaries.
on-arrival: ko_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 1; party_unity -= 2; progressive_credibility -= 4; public_trust -= 1; far_right_agenda += 3; coalition_blur += 3; ko_poll_momentum += 0.1; left_poll_momentum -= 0.3; metropolitan_liberals_left_affinity -= 2; liberal_professionals_left_affinity -= 3; urban_progressive_support -= 2; feminist_trust -= 2; news_headline = "A tactical ceasefire with KO lowers noise and weakens Lewica's progressive edge"

Back-channel talks cool the immediate barrage and restore some parliamentary
working contact. The price is political: movement organisers and younger
progressives hear us trading clarity for temporary peace with a larger party
that can restart the same line whenever the next dispute arrives.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@ko_media_smear_material
title: Ignore the frame and pivot to wages, housing and services
subtitle: Keep message discipline and let the smear run mostly unanswered in liberal media.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 2; ko_relation -= 3; progressive_credibility -= 3; public_trust -= 2; far_right_agenda += 4; coalition_blur += 1; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; metropolitan_liberals_left_affinity -= 5; liberal_professionals_left_affinity -= 4; workers_support += 1; anti_establishment_youth_left_affinity += 1; news_headline = "Lewica keeps a material line while the smear defines it for liberal audiences"

The campaign stays on rents, wages and public services instead of joining every
studio brawl. Some workers respect the discipline. But in the liberal media
ecosystem the unanswered label sticks, and the broader field still shifts a
step toward right-wing conflict frames.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

