= August 2023 — One hundred negotiations

Whatever arrangement we have just filed for the Sejm, the Senate is a separate
contest. Its one hundred seats are single-member districts: every committee
may nominate a candidate, but only the candidate with the most votes wins.

Donald Tusk's KO and the Third Way led by Szymon Hołownia and Władysław
Kosiniak-Kamysz can therefore divide the map between themselves. They need our
voters against PiS; they do not need to give our candidates a share of
winnable districts in return.

[? if senate_left_pact_mode = "full": Our polling and projected delegation are
large enough that excluding Lewica would endanger too many districts. We have
a seat at the table—but must decide whether the Senate bargain should remain
separate from the argument over one Sejm list.
?]

[? if senate_left_pact_mode = "outside": Our weak national position changes
the negotiation. KO and Third Way can field one agreed candidate while leaving
Lewica without an equal district quota. We cannot veto their bilateral pact;
we can prove that a few local organisations deserve exceptions, endorse their
map without reward, or run against it.
?]

- @senate_three_lists_pact
- @senate_one_list
- @senate_separate_lists
- @senate_weak_reservations
- @senate_weak_stand_down
- @senate_weak_run

@senate_three_lists_pact
title: Sign one four-party Senate Pact
subtitle: Czarzasty accepts a common map without reopening the Sejm-list bargain.
view-if: senate_left_pact_mode = "full"
