go-to: senate_three_lists_pact_aftermath

@senate_three_lists_pact_aftermath
title: One Senate map, one settled Sejm bargain

The negotiators put **KO, Polska 2050, PSL and Lewica** behind one candidate in
each allocated district. Włodzimierz Czarzasty can defend the agreement as
electoral arithmetic rather than submission to Donald Tusk: it does not alter
the legal form, branding or nomination control already settled for the Sejm.

Some local hopefuls lose their races before the ballot is printed. In return,
the districts assigned to Lewica carry the whole pact rather than only our
vote. We have exchanged breadth for winnability.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the common map

@senate_one_list
title: Demand one opposition list in both chambers
subtitle: Tusk gains an ally for one Sejm list; Third Way and Razem must defend refusing it.
view-if: senate_left_pact_mode = "full"
on-arrival: senate_pact_coordinated = 1; senate_pact_strength = 62; senate_pact_strategy = "Senate Pact strained by Lewica's one-list demand"; senate_left_pact_mode = "full"; senate_cohesion += 4; ko_relation += 5; psl_relation -= 5; p2050_relation -= 4; razem_dissent += 6; party_unity -= 3; opposition_list_pressure += 5; news_headline = "The Senate deal survives Lewica's demand for one Sejm list"
go-to: senate_one_list_aftermath

@senate_one_list_aftermath
title: The pact survives the larger argument

Donald Tusk welcomes our demand and immediately turns it against Third Way.
Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz refuse to dissolve their Sejm project; Razem says
a common Senate candidate is sensible precisely because it does **not** require
one proportional list under KO's leadership.

The district map is still signed, but later and with less trust. We gain a
clear answer to the one-list question: KO agrees, while Third Way and part of
our own party do not.

- @poland_event_queue: Campaign on the answer

@senate_separate_lists
title: Refuse the allocations and nominate separately
subtitle: Every Lewica organisation may campaign, even where it divides the anti-PiS vote.
view-if: senate_left_pact_mode = "full"
on-arrival: senate_pact_coordinated = 0; senate_pact_strength = 18; senate_pact_strategy = "Separate KO, Third Way and Lewica Senate slates"; senate_left_pact_mode = "outside"; senate_cohesion -= 14; party_unity += 2; ko_relation -= 5; psl_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 3; left_poll_momentum += 0.1; news_headline = "Lewica rejects the Senate allocations and files separately"
go-to: senate_separate_lists_aftermath

@senate_separate_lists_aftermath
title: Three names for one seat

County organisers no longer have to stand down for a nominee chosen in Warsaw.
Lewica posters appear even in districts assigned by KO and Third Way to their
own candidates, and the party briefly looks larger because it is visible
everywhere.

The ballot paper exposes the cost. Where PiS has one nominee, democratic voters
may now find three. A strong local Lewica campaign can win; a merely respectable
one can decide which rival loses.

- @poland_event_queue: File our candidates

@senate_weak_reservations
title: Prove that a few local organisations deserve candidates
subtitle: KO and Third Way keep the map; only demonstrated county strength can win exceptions.
view-if: senate_left_pact_mode = "outside"
choose-if: local_network >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: Our county network is too thin to make exclusion costly.
on-arrival: senate_pact_coordinated = 1; senate_pact_strength = 74; senate_pact_strategy = "KO–Third Way Senate Pact with limited Lewica reservations"; senate_left_pact_mode = "reserved"; senate_cohesion += 7; senate_left_leverage += 2; ko_relation += 1; psl_relation += 1; p2050_relation += 1; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Local strength wins Lewica a handful of places on the Senate map"
go-to: senate_weak_reservations_aftermath

@senate_weak_reservations_aftermath
title: Exceptions, not partnership

KO and Third Way refuse to reopen their national formula. They do, however,
yield a handful of districts where mayors, councillors and organisers can show
that a Lewica name is the pact's strongest name.

Those candidates receive the common endorsement. The rest of the map remains
a bilateral bargain, and Czarzasty has no equal veto over it. Local roots have
won representation that the national poll could not command.

- @poland_event_queue: Defend the reserved districts

@senate_weak_stand_down
title: Endorse the KO–Third Way map and stand down
subtitle: Maximise the anti-PiS vote while accepting no guaranteed Lewica districts.
view-if: senate_left_pact_mode = "outside"
on-arrival: senate_pact_coordinated = 1; senate_pact_strength = 78; senate_pact_strategy = "KO–Third Way Senate Pact; Lewica stands down"; senate_left_pact_mode = "stand_down"; senate_cohesion += 8; ko_relation += 3; psl_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 2; party_unity -= 5; left_poll_momentum -= 0.2; news_headline = "Lewica endorses a Senate map negotiated by KO and Third Way"
go-to: senate_weak_stand_down_aftermath

@senate_weak_stand_down_aftermath
title: Discipline without a district share

Tusk, Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz publish the map they negotiated together.
We endorse its candidates and withdraw competing nominations, so the pact can
collect much of our vote without placing Lewica on the ballot.

The democratic camp praises our discipline. Inside the party, organisers ask
what exactly loyalty has bought them. We may help elect an opposition Senate
majority while arriving in that chamber with no senators of our own.

- @poland_event_queue: Campaign against PiS

@senate_weak_run
title: Run Lewica candidates against the bilateral pact
subtitle: KO and Third Way still coordinate with each other; we make them compete for our voters.
view-if: senate_left_pact_mode = "outside"
on-arrival: senate_pact_coordinated = 1; senate_pact_strength = 68; senate_pact_strategy = "KO–Third Way Senate Pact with a separate Lewica slate"; senate_left_pact_mode = "outside"; senate_cohesion -= 8; party_unity += 2; ko_relation -= 6; psl_relation -= 4; p2050_relation -= 4; left_poll_momentum += 0.1; news_headline = "Lewica files candidates against the KO–Third Way Senate Pact"
go-to: senate_weak_run_aftermath

@senate_weak_run_aftermath
title: A bilateral pact, challenged from the Left

KO and Third Way keep one agreed nominee in every district they have divided.
Lewica files its own candidates beside them. We recover a platform for rents,
wages and public services, but we do not dissolve their pact by refusing it.

Every close count will now carry the same accusation: if PiS wins with less
than the combined democratic vote, our candidacy will be blamed. The only clean
answer is to win somewhere ourselves.

- @poland_event_queue: Print the separate ballots

@september_visa
# prose-audit: Grade A — Wawrzyk, Rau, consular staff and visa applicants make the scandal concrete; each Lewica line now leaves a retained legal, administrative or racial consequence.
title: The visa scandal
subtitle: Border rhetoric meets a consular patronage system
