= December 2023 — The keys, the signal and the law

KO leader Donald Tusk wants the old television command broken before it can
turn the transfer of power into a daily campaign against the new majority.
Maciej Świrski, chair of the National Broadcasting Council, insists that the
PiS-era boards remain lawful. President **[+ president_name +]** holds a veto
over any durable statute.

Journalists and technicians inside TVP, Polish Radio and PAP are receiving
rival instructions while viewers are asked to choose which newsroom is real.
[? if left_in_government: Our ministers can support a rapid corporate change,
accept the presidential veto wall or seek a temporary board. Each route makes
Lewica responsible for what happens to the staff and the law.?][? if not
left_in_government: The cabinet, not Lewica, controls the companies. We can
audit its route, put a statute beside it or build an outside monitor; we cannot
change a board by opposition declaration.?]

- @media_fast
- @media_statute
- @media_interim
- @media_opposition_ledger
- @media_opposition_bill
- @media_opposition_monitor

@media_fast
title: Back the rapid corporate route and publish every legal opinion
subtitle: Change management before PiS can regroup; accept litigation, rival boards and a ready-made audience for Republika.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: public_media_transition = "Rapid corporate transition"; public_media_patron = "ko"; media_capacity += 5; government_delivery += 4; government_procedural_restraint -= 5; legal_dualism += 4; president_relation -= 7; republika_capacity += 7; pis_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "Public media changes hands quickly and the legal challenge begins"

New managers enter the buildings under corporate resolutions and the signal
changes before the old boards accept dismissal. Staff can return to work under
one newsroom, but courts and rival regulators now receive competing claims to
the same institution.

PiS loses its broadcaster and gains a story about seizure. Presenters and
viewers move together toward Republika; speed has settled control for tonight,
not legality for the next government.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the contested transfer to the events desk

@media_statute
title: Insist on a statute, open appointments and a likely veto
subtitle: Let public hearings establish the mandate; partisan management and the President's veto can outlast the process.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: public_media_transition = "Statutory reform behind the veto wall"; public_media_patron = "pis"; constitutional_restraint += 6; government_procedural_restraint += 5; media_capacity -= 3; president_relation += 2; pis_relation += 2; republika_capacity += 4; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The coalition chooses a slower public-media mandate"

The coalition publishes appointment rules, opens hearings and sends a bill
through the Sejm. Journalists can see the institution being designed, but the
PiS-era managers remain in place while it is designed around them.

The President may still veto the finished law. We preserve a clean route to
reform and concede weeks of broadcasting to people who call patience weakness.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the public-media bill on the events desk

@media_interim
title: Offer the Palace a time-limited pluralist board
subtitle: Requires a functioning presidential channel. Share temporary appointments with the Palace; postpone the final settlement and anger KO.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
choose-if: left_in_government = 1 and (president_relation >= 30 or presidential_channel_open = 1)
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace sees no reason to share control.
on-arrival: public_media_transition = "Interim pluralist board"; public_media_patron = "neutral"; president_relation += 7; constitutional_restraint += 4; media_capacity += 1; ko_relation -= 3; progressives_dissent += 3; republika_capacity += 2; news_headline = "A temporary media truce preserves rival voices and postpones the final law"

The Palace and coalition divide a temporary board between professional and
political nominees, with an expiry date written into the agreement. Staff get
one chain of command and conservative viewers do not lose every familiar
voice overnight.

Tusk's party says we traded the transfer mandate for presidential consent.
The truce prevents a dual broadcaster by postponing the fight that would decide
who owns it permanently.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the temporary board on the events desk

@media_opposition_ledger
title: Publish the legal opinions and appointments ledger
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Name every appointment and disputed opinion without pretending an opposition audit can replace management.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The parliamentary team cannot complete the audit.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; public_media_transition = "KO transition under opposition legal audit"; public_media_patron = "ko"; media_capacity += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica audits the media transfer without claiming executive control"

Our lawyers publish who appointed each board, which corporate power the
cabinet invoked and where the opinions disagree. Dismissed workers and new
managers can both correct the record; KO can no longer hide speed behind a
press-conference phrase.

The audit changes no lock and appoints no editor. It gives courts, unions and
the public a chronology that belongs neither to PiS nor to the cabinet.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the independent ledger on the events desk

@media_opposition_bill
title: Table a pluralist appointments statute
subtitle: Make KO and the President answer a complete alternative; opposition authorship still cannot put it into force.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: public_media_transition = "Opposition pluralism bill beside the KO transition"; public_media_patron = "ko"; constitutional_restraint += 4; media_capacity += 1; ko_relation += 1; president_relation += 1; news_headline = "Lewica records a statutory alternative from outside cabinet"

Lewica tables open board appointments, protected newsroom terms and a funding
rule that neither government advertising nor a friendly council can quietly
rewrite. KO must explain what it accepts; the President must explain what he
would veto.

The text is a parliamentary offer, not a transfer of executive power. We gain
a standard against which to judge the cabinet and no control over tomorrow's
broadcast.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the pluralist statute to the events desk

@media_opposition_monitor
title: Build an independent transition-monitoring desk
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Keep unions, media lawyers and regional stations under observation; spend party capacity on scrutiny rather than reach.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
