= December 2023 — The election did not change the newsroom

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** still controls the executive and Maciej
Świrski still chairs the National Broadcasting Council. PiS-era managers keep
the public signal while presenters describe the election result as an attack
on the state.

Lewica has votes, lawyers and an audience of its own; it does not have the
company keys. We can map patronage, force a statutory alternative into the
record or stop borrowing distribution from institutions the government owns.

- @media_pis_audit
- @media_pis_statute
- @media_pis_build

@media_pis_audit
title: Publish an appointments and procurement ledger
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Follow managers, contracts and state advertising; scrutiny can expose control but cannot transfer it.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The parliamentary and legal team is already committed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; media_capacity += 4; public_trust += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; pis_relation -= 4; news_headline = "Opposition scrutiny maps public-media patronage without pretending to control it"

Procurement notices, board appointments and state-company advertising enter a
public ledger. Regional journalists and losing bidders give the patronage map
names which a general accusation never had.

The management survives and now knows it is being watched. We expose the chain
of control without telling viewers that an opposition committee has broken it.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the patronage ledger on the events desk

@media_pis_statute
title: Draft a pluralist statute and make the Palace choose
subtitle: Offer open appointments to government and President; a recorded alternative may still die before changing one newsroom.
on-arrival: public_media_transition = "Opposition pluralism bill"; public_media_patron = "pis"; constitutional_restraint += 4; president_relation += 1; pis_relation -= 2; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "A pluralist media bill creates a recorded parliamentary alternative"

The bill separates board terms from the electoral calendar and opens the
appointments. PiS must vote against the rule it claims already exists, and the
President must choose whether party control is worth an explicit veto.

Until a majority passes it, the proposal remains paper. It gives future reform
a lawful first draft, not today's editors an independent instruction.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the pluralist bill to the events desk

@media_pis_build
title: Build an independent Left distribution network
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Own the next broadcast and its bills; leave the state institution under PiS while building beyond it.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot capitalise an alternative outlet.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; media_capacity += 7; local_network += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The Left answers state broadcasting with an institution it actually controls"

Local correspondents, union media and the parliamentary studio begin sharing
one distribution system. It is smaller than TVP and cannot be dismissed by a
minister because the party now owns the equipment and subscriber list.

PiS keeps public broadcasting. We stop treating access to it as our media
strategy and accept the cost of becoming a publisher as well as a party.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the new network on the events desk

@independence_2023
# prose-audit: Grade A — Malewski, marchers, monitors and coalition negotiators replace the old organisation ledger; each Lewica choice now retains who gains the street and who bears the risk.
title: The 2023 Independence Day reckoning
subtitle: A delayed report from the street
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 15
order: 40
max-visits: 1
