= February 2024 — The empty chair is also content

Krzysztof Stanowski, the sports journalist and internet entrepreneur behind
Kanał Zero, offers politicians hours to speak and seconds in which to regret
it. His launch is not a party and does not need a manifesto: the audience, the
editing room and the invitation list are already power.

The invitation reaches a Lewica operating through **[+ media_relationship +]**.
A party with reporters can prepare an appearance and reuse it; a party built
around bookings is once again borrowing somebody else's public. We can send a
labour voice into the interview, refuse the host's terms, or begin treating him
as a broker whose favour must be maintained.

- @zero_prepare
- @zero_refuse
- @zero_court

@zero_prepare
title: Send a prepared labour voice into the long interview
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Put Dziemianowicz-Bąk through a hostile brief and keep the full answer ready when the short clip travels.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No briefing team can protect the appearance.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; media_relationship = "Prepared engagement with creator media"; media_capacity += 5; labor_credibility += 3; public_trust += 2; kanal_zero_capacity += 2; news_headline = "A prepared Left interview survives the clip economy"

Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk, Lewica's public-services and labour voice, arrives
with workplace cases, costed answers and a team cutting the full exchange while
Stanowski's editors cut theirs. The sharpest clip still belongs to the host;
the argument around it does not.

Young viewers meet a Left politician able to stay in the room. Kanał Zero gains
the legitimacy of a serious guest, and we gain material our own channels can
keep using after its front page moves on.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the prepared interview on the events desk

@zero_refuse
title: Refuse personality media and publish the programme directly
subtitle: Keep the party out of Stanowski's format; let Kanał Zero decide what the absent Left supposedly feared.
on-arrival: media_relationship = "Programme publishing outside creator media"; progressive_credibility += 1; media_capacity -= 3; kanal_zero_capacity += 4; young_support -= 2; news_headline = "Kanał Zero turns the empty chair into its own segment"

We publish the programme under our own name and decline the booking. Members
who distrust personality media get a clean rule: access is not the same thing
as accountability.

Stanowski films the empty chair, reads selected passages himself and asks why
Lewica would not defend them. We own every word of the document and almost none
of the conversation in which new viewers first encounter it.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the empty-chair decision to the events desk

@zero_court
title: Give Stanowski access and treat him as another political broker
subtitle: Keep invitations open through private briefings and availability; the gatekeeper gains leverage the party cannot audit.
on-arrival: media_relationship = "Brokered access through Kanał Zero"; media_capacity += 2; public_trust -= 1; kanal_zero_capacity += 5; barons_dissent -= 1; young_support += 1; news_headline = "The Left enters a relationship with a gatekeeper it cannot control"

Senior figures return calls, offer advance briefings and make themselves
available when Kanał Zero wants a guest. The interviews become less surprising
and the invitations more regular.

No payment changes hands, but access acquires a price in attention and
deference. The old apparatus likes a relationship it understands; voters who
expected us to challenge media power see another private court being attended.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the brokered relationship on the events desk

@local_election_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Czarzasty, Biedroń and the local organisers now receive a political verdict rather than a model explanation, with retained aftermaths for rebuilding, dependence or purge.
title: The local-election verdict
subtitle: Organisation, polling and local alliances now change the result
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 29
order: 10
