const euRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 5) - 2;
Q.eu_left_result =
    Math.max(
        2,
        Math.min(
            18,
            Math.round(
                (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) +
                (Number(Q.eu_campaign_progress) || 0) * 0.7 +
                (Number(Q.eu_influence) || 0) * 0.025 +
                euRoll * 0.4
            )
        )
    );
Q.eu_konf_result =
    Math.max(
        3,
        Math.min(
            24,
            Math.round(
                (Number(Q.konf_poll) || 0) +
                (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) * 0.05 -
                (Number(Q.far_right_split) || 0) * 0.03 -
                euRoll * 0.3
            )
        )
    );
Q.eu_election_outcome =
    Q.eu_left_result >= Q.eu_konf_result
        ? "Left advance"
        : (Q.eu_left_result + 3 >= Q.eu_konf_result
            ? "close contest"
            : "radical-right advantage");
Q.eu_right_shift_done = 1;
Q.eu_progressive_headwind += 8;
Q.democratic_rightward_pressure += 3;
Q.far_right_agenda += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "European vote: Left " + Q.eu_left_result +
    "%, Konfederacja " + Q.eu_konf_result + "%";
!}

= June 2024 — [+ eu_election_outcome +]

Robert Biedroń, New Left co-chair and incumbent MEP, reads the count beside
Lewica candidates Krzysztof Śmiszek and Joanna Scheuring-Wielgus. The Left has
**[+ eu_left_result +]%**; Konfederacja has **[+ eu_konf_result +]%**.

Across the Union, the centre-right EPP remains the largest group, nationalist
and radical-right parties gain ground, and the Greens and liberals retreat.
The centrist majority survives, but every progressive Polish reform now meets
an **8-point European headwind**: fewer willing allies, a more conservative
agenda and more room for Polish coalition partners to demand delay.

[? if eu_election_outcome = "Left advance": The delegation can claim that a
social Europe still mobilises voters beyond the coalition's liberal centre.?]
[? if eu_election_outcome = "close contest": Two incompatible answers to
European integration have emerged from the count almost level.?][? if
eu_election_outcome = "radical-right advantage": Sławomir Mentzen's
Konfederacja leaves with the larger insurgent audience and every governing
party is tempted to imitate its migration language.?]

Our choice is whether to separate from the coalition on material policy, close
ranks around democratic normalisation, cash in years of European organising or
chase the rival frame which just prospered.

- @eu_left
- @eu_coalition
- @eu_network
- @eu_right

@eu_left
title: Differentiate on wages, housing and public investment
subtitle: Make Biedroń's delegation a social opposition inside Europe; coalition liberals will resist the spending line.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 5; eu_left_network += 4; eu_campaign_progress += 1 if eu_social_mission = 0; eu_social_mission = 1; eu_influence += 3; eu_progressive_headwind -= 2; ko_relation -= 3; psl_relation -= 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.3; left_poll_momentum += 0.1 if eu_campaign_progress >= 3; razem_cooperation += 3; fiscal_stress += 2; news_headline = "The Left answers the radical right with material conflict"

Biedroń, Śmiszek and Scheuring-Wielgus take wages, housing funds and public
investment into their European group rather than presenting another defence of
the status quo. Razem can recognise the conflict and union partners gain a
delegation asking what integration pays at work.

KO and PSL object to commitments whose bill returns to Warsaw. We recover a
reason to vote Left in a pro-European electorate and reopen the coalition's
argument over who finances it.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the social-European line on the events desk

@eu_coalition
title: Close ranks around European normalisation
subtitle: Present rule of law and restored influence as the common victory; Razem will ask where the distinct Left programme went.
on-arrival: eu_institutional_trust += 4; eu_influence += 3; ko_relation += 6; p2050_relation += 4; government_coalition_dissent -= 3; party_unity -= 2; razem_dissent += 4; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "European normalisation becomes the coalition's common shelter"

The governing parties appear together and describe restored European access,
rule-of-law repair and support for Ukraine as one democratic achievement.
Voters tired of the PiS conflict see a government speaking with one voice.

Lewica gains influence through the coalition and loses the argument for why
that influence required a separate Left ballot. Razem records the absence;
partners bank the calm.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the coalition line to the events desk

@eu_network
title: Turn the accumulated European network into a Polish social-security campaign
subtitle: Requires three European channels and 42 influence. Bring unions, Ukraine allies and parliamentary contacts home as one recognisably Left compact.
choose-if: eu_campaign_progress >= 3 and eu_influence >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: The earlier European campaign did not build enough leverage.
view-if: eu_campaign_progress >= 2
on-arrival: eu_campaign_complete = 1; eu_campaign_stage = "Polish EU settlement — funds, democratic law and social investment"; eu_influence += 8; eu_left_network += 5; eu_progressive_headwind -= 4; ukraine_solidarity += 4; labor_credibility += 4; military_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.5; party_unity += 2; far_right_agenda -= 2; news_headline = "Years of European work produce a distinct Polish Left campaign"

Trade union contacts, democratic-law allies and Ukrainian partners come
to Warsaw under one compact. It ties social security to a state able to defend
both its border and its courts, instead of asking voters to choose between the
two.

The campaign exists only because earlier missions built people willing to sign
it. Konfederacja cannot dismiss the result as another Brussels slogan; the
Left has brought a network home and given it Polish obligations.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the Warsaw compact on the events desk

@eu_right
title: Harden the migration line before Konfederacja owns it
subtitle: Follow the issue which rewarded Mentzen's party; sacrifice refugee and minority trust without guaranteeing any voters follow us back.
on-arrival: border_security_confidence += 4; refugee_empathy -= 5; minority_safety -= 4; far_right_agenda += 6; konf_poll_momentum += 0.4; democratic_rightward_pressure += 5; eu_progressive_headwind += 3; eu_influence -= 3; eu_left_network -= 3; news_headline = "The governing parties chase a radical-right frame"

Our spokespeople move from wages and institutions to the claim that the
coalition must be harder on migration than Konfederacja expects. The change
reassures voters who read the European count principally as a border warning.

Mentzen welcomes the concession and asks why they should buy the copy. Refugee
and minority organisations hear their security traded for an electorate that
may still prefer the original.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the rightward turn to the events desk

