= September 2024 — The classroom, the rent queue and the rumour

Support for Ukrainian refugees has fallen to a bare majority. Families who
arrived after the invasion are still working, studying and waiting for the war
to end; Polish parents and tenants are also waiting for school places, housing
and appointments from services already short of staff.

Konfederacja leader Sławomir Mentzen calls that scarcity proof of preference.
New Left co-chair Włodzimierz Czarzasty must decide whether our answer is more
capacity, one transparent rule for everyone, or a promise to remove advantages
we have not first proved exist.

[? if left_in_government: We can fund services and own their delivery.?][? if
not left_in_government: We can organise municipal evidence and table funding;
cabinet and councils still control implementation.?] In either role, repeating
the rumour will change who feels safe long before it changes a benefit rule.

- @refugee_services
- @refugee_rules
- @refugee_echo

@refugee_services
