    Q.household_security += 4;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Receiving communities receive capacity instead of another slogan";
} else {
    Q.refugee_settlement =
        "Opposition municipal-capacity amendment";
    Q.local_network += 4;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Lewica documents municipal needs and tables funding from opposition";
}
!}

[? if left_in_government: Receiving municipalities gain service money tied to
classrooms, housing and labour inspection. Polish residents and Ukrainian
families encounter additional capacity rather than a contest over the same
unchanged queue.?][? if not left_in_government: Our councils publish shortages
and a funded amendment while local organisers assemble the case. We can make
the cabinet answer the need; we cannot spend its budget.?]

Employers exploiting refugee labour face the same inspectors who protect local
wages. Solidarity acquires staff and buildings instead of depending on public
goodwill alone.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the receiving-community package on the events desk

@refugee_rules
title: Publish equal benefit and workplace rules for everyone
subtitle: A public rules proposal reduces rumours; household delivery still belongs to the cabinet and municipalities.
on-arrival: refugee_settlement = "Equal and transparent benefit rules proposal"; public_trust += 3; labor_credibility += 2; refugee_empathy += 2; anti_ukrainian_pressure -= 2; household_policy_pressure += 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Lewica parliamentary and public campaign"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Transparent rules reduce the market for benefit rumours"

Lewica publishes eligibility, waiting-list and workplace rules in Polish and
Ukrainian and demands that councils report how they apply them. A rumour about
preference can now be checked against a rule bearing a responsible office.

The proposal does not add a flat or teacher and does not administer a benefit.
It gives residents a shared standard and the cabinet a concrete transparency
demand which can later be measured against delivery.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the equal-rules proposal on the events desk

