= October 2024 — The junior partner moves inside the party

PiS and Suwerenna Polska sign a merger agreement and ideological declaration.
Ill **Zbigniew Ziobro** remains the outgoing party leader; **Patryk Jaki** signs
for his organisation. The incoming authority is **Jarosław Kaczyński**, whose
PiS apparatus now contains the former junior partner as an organised current.

Ziobro once used a separate party and a handful of deputies to veto policy
inside the United Right. After the 2023 defeat, that independence offers fewer
offices and more exposure. Jaki's sovereigntists, former justice-ministry
officials and judicial hardliners now prefer Kaczyński's treasury, candidate
lists and legal machine. The Morawiecki technocrats who remain inside PiS see
the bargain differently: the party is acquiring discipline by importing the
faction which helped make it unelectable.

For Lewica, the merger makes it harder to isolate Ziobro's record from PiS,
but easier to demand common responsibility for courts, prosecutors and blocked
EU funds. It also plants a harder sovereigntist bloc inside the future PiS
succession.
[? if left_in_government = 1 and government_party = "pis": In this timeline
Lewica sits inside the PiS-led cabinet. Jaki's people are therefore becoming
our governing partners, and any demand for accountability also tests how much
of Ziobro's inheritance our ministers are willing to serve beside.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1 and government_party != "pis": From a democratic
cabinet, Lewica can connect scrutiny of the merger to an institutional record
it now has the authority to repair.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: From opposition, Lewica can investigate and
campaign, but cannot present a programme as a government act.?]

- @sovereign_merger_record
- @sovereign_merger_factions
- @sovereign_merger_social

@sovereign_merger_record
title: Publish one court-and-prosecution record for the merged party
subtitle: Treat absorption as an admission that Kaczyński and Ziobro share responsibility.
on-arrival: sovereign_merger_response = "Joint accountability for the justice record"; judicial_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_restraint += 2; pis_relation -= 5; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "Lewica makes the merger an admission of shared responsibility"

Lewica publishes a single chronology of appointments, disciplinary cases and
prosecutorial interventions, signed with both party names. Jaki cannot inherit
PiS protection while presenting Ziobro's ministry as somebody else's record;
Kaczyński cannot call the merger organisational housekeeping while disowning
the people he has absorbed. PiS closes ranks, but the demand for accountability
now has one address.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the common record on the events desk

@sovereign_merger_factions
title: Track Jaki's hardliners and Morawiecki's critics separately
subtitle: Read the new party as a contest over succession, not a single obedient machine.
on-arrival: sovereign_merger_response = "Separate channels to PiS internal blocs"; media_capacity += 2; coalition_opportunity_pis += 2; public_trust -= 1; pis_relation += 1; news_headline = "Lewica maps the conflict hidden by PiS consolidation"

Our researchers begin keeping two calendars: Jaki's rallies and judicial
campaigns on one, Morawiecki's economic conferences and cautious European
signals on the other. Journalists gain a map of the quarrel hidden beneath the
same logo, and future votes may expose it. The price is suspicion among our own
supporters that we are scouting partners inside a party whose record we once
treated as indivisible.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the faction map on the events desk

